    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 301129\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n429 AM PDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Mild weather and warming temperatures are expected through the \n  weekend into early next week. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through Tuesday.\n\nRidging will build over the region as the trough responsible for \nMonday and Tuesday's storms moves into New Mexico today. Rising \n500 mb heights will allow for temperatures across the area to \nrebound, with warmer than normal temperatures returning by \nThursday. In addition to warmer than normal temperatures, lighter \nwinds and dry conditions will also accompany this ridge. Weather \nwill remain warm and mild through the weekend. Long term guidance \nshows a shortwave trough approaching the West Coast as we head \ninto next week, which will result in southerly breezes and \nincreased cloud cover. \n\n&&\n\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Cloud \ncover continues to thin with light winds becoming breezy further \ninto the morning. Expect gusty northwest winds peaking above 20kts \nuntil the late morning before reducing slightly and turning more \nnortherly. Gusts cut off by the mid afternoon and winds become more \nmoderate. By the late afternoon winds become light and variable and \nstay that way through the remainder of the TAF period.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Breezy to gusty \nnortherly winds affect KVGT through the morning with gusts holding \noff at KHND, KDAG, and KIFP until the late morning/ Early afternoon \nwhile other TAF sites keep weak winds. Winds across the region look \nto become light before sunset. Expect mostly clear skies through the \nTAF period. \n\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Stessman\nAVIATION...Murdock\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
